Third-party data
- data/pairs_train.parquet, data/pairs_selection.parquet, data/pairs_test.parquet contain headline pairs derived from the
  Upworthy Research Archive (J. Nathan Matias, Kevin Munger, Marianne Aubin Le Quere and Charles Ebersole, "The Upworthy
  Research Archive, a time series of 32,487 experiments in U.S. media", Scientific Data 8, 195 (2021),
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-021-00934-7; data at https://osf.io/jd64p/), licensed CC BY 4.0. Our changes: tests
  in the maintainers' date window for unreliable randomisation removed, within-test pairs of headlines with the same
  image built, click-rate z-scores added (scripts/build_pairs.py).
- News articles come from the cc_news dataset (Hugging Face vblagoje/cc_news, built with news-please). Their text and
  titles are NOT redistributed here: data/ only lists our article ids, split, domain, date and SHA-256 hashes, and
  results/final/final_human.parquet carries no title text. scripts/build_articles.py rebuilds the articles from the public
  dataset; the cc_news licence on the dataset card is "unknown", so check it before redistributing rebuilt text.

The code (scripts/, reproduce.py, paper/make_fig_stages.py) is licensed separately under the MIT licence (see LICENSE).
